From 7b23fdd795793642f0255e64525d54458ac2f7f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (sandbox)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 17:05:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(frontend): route API calls through VITE_API_BASE_URL for
 split-origin deploy

The frontend (Cloudflare Pages) and backend (Render) are deployed to
different origins in production. Raw fetch("/api/...") calls and the
generated API client both used relative paths, which resolved against
the frontend's own origin instead of the backend, causing profile
loading and other API calls to fail with 'Profilni yuklab bo'lmadi'.

- Add apiUrl(path) helper (src/lib/api-url.ts) that prefixes relative
  paths with VITE_API_BASE_URL when set, or leaves them unchanged when
  empty/unset (preserves same-origin local dev behavior).
- Wire all 8 raw fetch("/api/...") call sites in App.tsx through apiUrl().
- Initialize the generated @workspace/api-client-react client's base URL
  via setBaseUrl() at startup (main.tsx), using the same env var.
- Document VITE_API_BASE_URL in .env.example.

No backend, CORS, Firebase, database, or Telegram changes.
